    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** (82.69) and **James Wood** (78.42) serving as our primary engines. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a high-floor matchup against Pallante, where his elite sprint speed is maximized by the pitcher's slow delivery to the plate. Meanwhile, **James Wood** is our strongest play against a struggling Jacob Lopez (5.64 xERA); his elite 0.433 xwOBA and top-of-the-order positioning provide an ideal foundation for run production. **Isaac Paredes** (70.71) also offers significant value, as his strong platoon edge against Young allows him to punch well above his base projection despite a slight park penalty.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the final bench spots, with **Henry Bolte** (48.02) narrowly missing the cut. While **Henry Bolte** benefits from a favorable park, the optimizer preferred the superior matchup density found in the starters; he was ultimately squeezed out by the consistency of players like **Zach McKinstry** and **Cole Young**, whose roles are more solidified in the lineup order. We are also monitoring **Mickey Moniak** (64.11) closely; while his matchup against the elite Greene is statistically daunting (2.51 xERA), his massive +14% park factor and platoon advantage make him a high-variance, high-reward play that could break the slate if he connects on a mistake. \n\nManagement flags remain in effect for the majority of our squad, as many players, including **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Cole Young**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Corbin Carroll**, are currently subject to \"Lineup Pending\" status. While we have projected based on historical batting order, any mid-day shifts to lower-value lineup spots could dampen the efficiency of these assets. Furthermore, **Dalton Rushing** (40.20) sits at our absolute floor for starting consideration; we are essentially banking on his platoon advantage to mitigate the threat posed by Schlittler. We will continue to monitor weather and official lineups to ensure no benchable assets are forced into starts due to late scratches.",
